{"title":"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Simplified_Explanation_-_Grade_7_Level)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Simplified Explanation - Grade 7 Level)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the greatest power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f92a8ab255792f3d76b80db750016716a1c2e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{1002} - 4^{501}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/e/eee800fd17e301b2f46ecd595adfc332f69ae13a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 2^{1002} \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 2^{1003} \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 2^{1004} \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 2^{1005} \\qquad\\textbf{(E) }2^{1006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"488\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We begin by factoring the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1ac6e3c169b3181a19efa8db6772db74e5a194f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1002}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> out. This leaves us with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/6/7864bbe9ab875257661bf26b7d1e6d9dba82d89c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{1002} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>We factor the difference of squares, leaving us with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/52916ca631a31eb50bb8d8f53a26fd3ef81962d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5^{501} - 1)(5^{501} + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" />. We note that all even powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than two end in ...<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/15117013d1b9a82a24e57d2e8d7ffa4b5df7bb85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$625$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. Also, all odd powers of five more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> end in  ...<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b829a6f0810a25e9ca9f85d690f2bafd0f2c1773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/9/d29020172de33adefba0ef346436479faffb42a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5^{501} + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"19\" /> would end in ...<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bb4795bbf9125d08b3ddc9fbe238166da3bb450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$126$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> and thus would contribute one power of two to the answer, but not more. \n</p><p>We can continue to factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/42618132c21a9c69a4934a507c96f28663de8e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5^{501} - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"19\" /> as a difference of cubes, leaving us with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/303b8572235f57086e0558ecc65d3308ff13c3f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5^{167} - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"19\" /> times an odd number (Notice that the other number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae130093158049576302a7bd05945218be7cf81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{334} + 5^{167} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" />. The powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> end in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the two powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will end with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will make it end in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, this is an odd number). <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/303b8572235f57086e0558ecc65d3308ff13c3f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5^{167} - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"19\" /> ends in ...<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/c/71c1636bd2876630688f77deef38f6203e8a5875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$124$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, contributing two powers of two to the final result.\n</p><p>Or we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/42618132c21a9c69a4934a507c96f28663de8e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5^{501} - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"19\" /> ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/c/71c1636bd2876630688f77deef38f6203e8a5875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$124$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, and is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> only. Still that's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Adding these extra <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers of two to the original <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/a/63a8720f439e8e8887a0746430412c323e81e13c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1002$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> factored out, we obtain the final answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f20ca6e6775d8c233dee9c329773ea38df1c718c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D) } 2^{1005}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can write the expression in a more primitive form which will allow us to start factoring.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a8d51a3defb7f8e69586a5018d0bc1e14a11df3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10^{1002} - 4^{501} = 2^{1002} \\cdot 5^{1002} - 2^{1002}\\]\" width=\"262\" height=\"15\" />\nNow, we can factor out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1ac6e3c169b3181a19efa8db6772db74e5a194f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1002}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" />. This leaves us with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/6/7864bbe9ab875257661bf26b7d1e6d9dba82d89c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{1002} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />. Call this number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, our final answer will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/1/1e1815578b1f5ec8d12e88c4672de8a230716e8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1002+k}$\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the largest power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Now we can consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f5d8f4178c5f1306f36f493f893a9f7a62829a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N \\pmod{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/6088be3d938441de5370e3109df6a928106d432e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\le 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> by the answer choices. \n</p><p>Note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/9/5b9243dfe49c73f6725030f7506d9bfc33dd9ce9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 5^1 &amp;\\equiv 5 \\pmod{16} \\\\ 5^2 &amp;\\equiv 9 \\pmod{16} \\\\ 5^3 &amp;\\equiv 13 \\pmod{16} \\\\ 5^4 &amp;\\equiv 1 \\pmod{16} \\\\ 5^5 &amp;\\equiv 5 \\pmod{16} \\\\ &amp;\\: \\: \\qquad \\vdots \\end{align*}\" width=\"148\" height=\"165\" />\nThe powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cycle in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906effc8d65841dc2d0d8c3cae84f6dff0d27c39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> with a period of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/5/705cfe93c4af7eb5de20eb772eef1fe2f0fc49fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^{1002} \\equiv 5^2 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{16} \\implies 5^{1002} - 1 \\equiv 8 \\pmod{16}\\]\" width=\"441\" height=\"19\" />\nThis means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13a2e8fb43ccdc50865c7f581a975f750700198d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8= 2^3$\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> but not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/c/7ac182d9cd58a044efd8082b5617115dba421342.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 = 2^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f96a3de68cfb881f4b3cc002ec222bba93f1e16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> which is 3 more 2 and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83de1d157e43676c91e321716d310bc704cc5f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1002 + 3} =\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\: 2^{1005}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"159\" height=\"31\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Convert <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/5/fe5641d678c30c182b690dcafe6f85f7deda1ace.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^{501}=2^{1002}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" />. We can factor out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1ac6e3c169b3181a19efa8db6772db74e5a194f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1002}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> to get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaafa67242c9d0ba7fe2e0edb2463b07eb85a403.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_2(10^{1002}-2^{1002})=1002+\\nu_2(5^{1002}-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"318\" height=\"21\" />. Using the adjusted Lifting The Exponent lemma (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/2/3428c236c5b65d892dba6d002b24bd2137bd13fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_2(a^n-b^n)=\\nu_2(n)+\\nu_2(a^2-b^2)-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"291\" height=\"19\" /> for all even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and odd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />), we get that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9ca26d253a0ec32e1eaffd369c24a1b26633a54a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1002+\\nu_2(1002)+\\nu_2(24)-1}=2^{1002+1+3-1}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}2^{1005}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"373\" height=\"31\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Factor out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1ac6e3c169b3181a19efa8db6772db74e5a194f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1002}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/8/558135880e6fe8d87eb96bfebb107a2411ec8b93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1002}(5^{1002} - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"19\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f44453bce5bc78fd1ea1dc3b326e59500dced61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{1002}-1\\equiv (-3)^{1002}-1\\equiv (9)^{501}-1\\equiv 1^{501}-1\\equiv 0\\pmod{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"480\" height=\"21\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb2cce094211fc56b2b8b831bbaa619bf298bf57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{1002}-1\\equiv 11^{1002}-1\\equiv 121\\cdot (11^4)^{250} - 1\\equiv 121 - 1\\equiv 8 \\pmod{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"524\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/d/2fd2e2479181778818dc05f1ab9f301ecda09920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{1002}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" /> has 3 factors of 2. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83a8e72a717008f5be09e7ec6a6a1fc483441944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1002 + 3} =\\boxed{2^{1005}(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"157\" height=\"33\" /> is the largest power of two which divides the given number\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like Solution 1, factor out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1ac6e3c169b3181a19efa8db6772db74e5a194f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1002}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/ceafc079d99992dd4f72890b9a193cdd775b0263.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2^{1002})(5^{501}-1)(5^{501}+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"203\" height=\"21\" />. Using engineer's induction, we observe that for any positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an odd positive integer), it appears that the least even numbers directly above and below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> in value must contain a maximum multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and a maximum multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Hence, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/4/ee46c9d18d0053762734c45bccd887a444123a56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1002+2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ec33dfa288a4537efdbb161e34352c37e85d5b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} 2^{1005}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"79\" height=\"32\" /> .\n</p><p>Proof;\n</p><p>For all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2eab6e5b2b78a6b8e9849f0bd3b07e94456b1285.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=5^{n}$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> where n is an odd integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must end in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/214f2b60a5b2eeaaeefb9c8e24e4a26255190a60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> \nThus, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4baf6d4b1cfa69b68b3204b5e2eba0c5755fe20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccb103143393c0119f5ab61d6d53a852ce70fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> respectively end in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/c/71c1636bd2876630688f77deef38f6203e8a5875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$124$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/0237b3e89b95c00a35beedf8525f89cba1b753ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$126.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> \n</p><p>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />&#160;: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4baf6d4b1cfa69b68b3204b5e2eba0c5755fe20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We know that this number takes the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f65951a84bd3858470b381686eb32c48f093ee7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abcde... 124$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c850fa6c15da60232724cd75ab225a6dd814e8ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abcde...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer that ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/c/71c1636bd2876630688f77deef38f6203e8a5875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$124$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c850fa6c15da60232724cd75ab225a6dd814e8ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abcde...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times an even number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/c/71c1636bd2876630688f77deef38f6203e8a5875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$124$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/1/9e172a5f04e2fa000988b79863d3e51fe3861e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(31)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb16bfc3a50768461a7b417ebfb3da5789d9d25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98b2ca62dd4d54e6e62ebd3829abbf293d26213f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4e + 4 \\cdot 31 = 4(e+31) = 4o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"221\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3eabe6c97f03e413d1aa3c292e9478f286e64df1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$o$\" width=\"9\" height=\"8\" /> is an odd number\n</p><p>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />&#160;: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccb103143393c0119f5ab61d6d53a852ce70fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We know that this number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/9/b09844ed5175e98951e1fd7726543c14261cf0d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$fghijk...126$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" /> ends. Because it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4baf6d4b1cfa69b68b3204b5e2eba0c5755fe20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, which is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906cca155f13e01f51c7a5067bdaac37da6f846d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1 = 4o + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"15\" /> which is an even number that is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, it must have a maximum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>This means that for any number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> being in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/a/f0a1ae7267b12fc456ea9e4bd495e17b31c987cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{n}$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an odd integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4baf6d4b1cfa69b68b3204b5e2eba0c5755fe20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> must have a maximum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccb103143393c0119f5ab61d6d53a852ce70fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> must have a maximum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n~ShangJ2\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using difference of squares, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/7/8371060e7a6dc6e12394bd771e0dae4f81babbfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(10^{501}-2^{501}\\right) \\left(10^{501}+2^{501}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"219\" height=\"23\" />. Factoring a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dcc9e44c91a9257444081a92db7321bdf26a619.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{501}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"17\" /> out, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/1/a81571a7787394a43a9066b1eac45a11a106aeff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(2^{501}\\right) \\left(5^{501}-1\\right) \\left(2^{501}\\right) \\left(5^{501}+1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"258\" height=\"23\" />, and grouping like terms give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26be0e5f00be447e0a3d1411f3695145e202dfc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(2^{1002}\\right) \\left(5^{501}-1\\right) \\left(5^{501}+1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"215\" height=\"23\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nThen, you would go ahead and innocently choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/5/435ca070de37ea7a1ca9ec8bb43dd41ad620f943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 2^{1002}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"21\" />, right? No! Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is any odd integer greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, it always ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b829a6f0810a25e9ca9f85d690f2bafd0f2c1773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/374e2398452d0ecb630ceef21edd6906c03da015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{501}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bb4795bbf9125d08b3ddc9fbe238166da3bb450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$126$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8ebafb63ae165218374a897a96958c958ad54101.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{501}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/c/71c1636bd2876630688f77deef38f6203e8a5875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$124$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, so they add up to an extra three <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s. Therefore, the answer is actually <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/0/a9002016607043af6257a62919cec3b2c90b8a61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1002+3}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 2^{1005}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"163\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~MrThinker\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that we are trying to find the number of powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/08235c6c9175c4f0ba6eb633058f44bfc384a7db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5^{1002}-1) \\cdot 2^{1002}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"21\" /> Let's see how many <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/d/2fd2e2479181778818dc05f1ab9f301ecda09920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{1002}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" /> has.\n</p><p>Try the first 4 powers of 5, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50f9c72d91ec440826a71947c96d58c58318c97a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^1$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/369aa2b96d08192baf66da44577be596a58d6778.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cec0dcde3e88efde55a8c8df29fc970f9e6c6da8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/d/c5df324769ac1365d3b379a13a1f21c3333e9952.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^4$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />. Note that when taking mod 4, all result in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/842dac4a51f17d41ec6e1d1a3fc3fb845d8f5f8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\pmod 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />. When taking mod 8, even powers result in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/4/944022cdf47418795d06d85f0c2744fc278baf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />. When taking mod 16, every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th power (i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae7990a755d7439a9d17e97ec74f12dbe03b0808.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,8,..$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" />) will result in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/7/2f7b8bf84a36f77e1c210f0d598a9caa1fc703f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\pmod{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/a/63a8720f439e8e8887a0746430412c323e81e13c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1002$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is even but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/3/0c3fc1904c0ce824adc28e1e5f38c92cc0752055.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\pmod 4, 5^{1002}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"21\" /> will be equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/4/944022cdf47418795d06d85f0c2744fc278baf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> but not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77db0cddf0c5cc3ce8f8d66eddfaebec803aa90f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\pmod 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/6/7864bbe9ab875257661bf26b7d1e6d9dba82d89c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{1002} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" /> ≡ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/3/2c308ec8ec51fc42e90b06b590e8589504e64d48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\pmod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />, and so we have an extra power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f6a4ab443c94f13ae3ad0efbc8c6fa07b58a930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, hence the result is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/b/91b07fdce1ef515921b820d6142f7be4be8688c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1002+3=1005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />. Hence the answer is (D).\n</p><p>~mathboy282\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8\">Solution 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can rewrite the expression as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/619469eed170bb478a0629c9481852ee3f378ef7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1002} \\cdot 5^{1002} - 2^{1002}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />. Then factoring out a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1ac6e3c169b3181a19efa8db6772db74e5a194f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1002}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> gets us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/d/2fd2e2479181778818dc05f1ab9f301ecda09920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{1002}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />. Then we can factor it by using the difference of squares formula. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/b/05b09fe81dee0043eb0c13aa020a4b6c53d95568.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5^{501}-1)(5^{501}+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"21\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c68ddfa3184085838f46afa2265adce6a5dfa78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5^{501}+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"21\" /> can be factored out further by using the difference of cubes formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/949a8cea5cf8740c3f29e1a5d93e97d718411690.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{501}+1 = \\left(5^{167}\\right)^3 + 1^3 = \\left(5^{167}+1\\right)\\left(5^{334} - 5^{167} + 1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"413\" height=\"26\" />. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e874111a731905565c6cb475f90b226dbc6d70ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(5^{167}\\right)^3 + 1^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"94\" height=\"26\" /> ends with 6, so dividing by 2 gets a number that ends with 3, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/8/64853f9de6e5625f5927161606385f4c48c9b189.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{501} +1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> gets us 1 factor of 2. Now we deal with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce3d798dbf4aaa764a647a0bcd35ca19b77e907f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(5^{334} - 5^{167} + 1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/999d984e7a5a906408052029194f004275242cc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{334}, 5^{167},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are all odd numbers, and the sum of 3 odd numbers is odd, so there are no powers of 2 from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce3d798dbf4aaa764a647a0bcd35ca19b77e907f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(5^{334} - 5^{167} + 1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8ebafb63ae165218374a897a96958c958ad54101.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{501}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> can be factored into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/4/af4dcdcf126486476710fa76732434bf5e08751d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{501}-1 = (5-1)\\left(5^{500} + 5^{499} + \\cdots + 5^1 + 5^0\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"364\" height=\"23\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/6/0265d1d2bf3afa9c71702b6c7fbaf4749140331d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5-1=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> gets us 2 powers of 2. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/480c71b0d506b52ffaf8c83ef2993bd25abc71a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(5^{500} + 5^{499} + \\cdots + 5^1 + 5^0\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"221\" height=\"23\" /> is the sum of 501 odd numbers, so that is odd, which gets us no powers of 2. Therefore, in total, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/619469eed170bb478a0629c9481852ee3f378ef7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1002} \\cdot 5^{1002} - 2^{1002}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/9/7b98085bac4cb12744e64f85d91386c621f69741.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1002+1+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> factors of 2, which gets us the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8de641a309fc5878c26baf699f2382b7d4b02b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"29\" />\n</p><p>~biegetomcat72\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/aCtvD8nitgg\">https://youtu.be/aCtvD8nitgg</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Simplified_Explanation_-_Grade_7_Level.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Simplified_Explanation_-_Grade_7_Level)\">Video Solution (Simplified Explanation - Grade 7 Level)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Simplified Explanation - Grade 7 Level)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6mkzhgRAx9Q\">https://youtu.be/6mkzhgRAx9Q</a>\n</p><p>~Ace the olympiad\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B\">2014 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017144555\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.070 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.086 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 957/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 30306/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.995      1 -total\n 60.55%    7.868      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 38.49%    5.002      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12388:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017144555 and revision id 291816. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}